# App features

Optional desktop capabilities extend `Feature` from `$features/feature.svelte.ts`. Settings are the `features.<name>` slice of the central tree — not a second store.

```typescript
export class History extends Feature {
	name = 'history';
	enable() { /* start watchers */ }
	disable() { /* unsubscribe, clear timers */ }
	defaultSettings() {
		return { enabled: true };
	}
}

export const history = new History();
```

Wire it in three places:

1. Singleton export (above)
2. `app.register('history', history)` in `packages/app/src/routes/+layout.ts`
3. `Features` in `packages/app/src/app.d.ts`

Boot calls `feature.register()` (isolated errors). Auth is **not** a feature — use `app.features.auth` / `account`.

Do not start feature logic in a route `onMount` if it belongs in `enable()`. Do not persist feature settings outside `defaultSettings` + the central tree.
